  "step_3": "The decision reason requires evaluating and preferring the lottery with higher variance (Lottery B). However, the individual focuses solely on the higher probability of winning in Lottery A, which relates to the first moment (probability of success), not the second moment (variance). The information considered (winning chance) is unrelated to variance. Furthermore, the justification (greater chance to win) contradicts the rule of the decision reason, which would favor Lottery B due to its higher variance. There is no indication that variance was computed or considered. Therefore, it is certain that the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
